menu "PlantHub Integrations"

config PLANTHUB_INFLUX_TLS
    bool "Enable HTTPS for the InfluxDB client"
    default n
    help
        A policy switch, not a build switch: when enabled,
        integr_config_set() accepts https:// URLs in the Influx config
        in addition to http://. It does NOT gate anything at build
        time -- esp_http_client and esp-tls link into the firmware
        either way in this IDF config, so leaving this off does not
        save flash.

        Enabling it today buys you an HTTPS client with NO certificate
        verification wired up: no CA bundle, no pinning. The transport
        is encrypted but the server is not authenticated, which is not
        meaningfully stronger than the plain-http trusted-LAN model
        this project otherwise assumes (PlanV1 3.7). Certificate-bundle
        wiring is future work; until it lands, prefer http:// and only
        turn this on if you understand and accept that gap. The MQTT
        client is unaffected either way (always plain mqtt:// in v1).

endmenu
